  "interpretations": [
    "Inspected DsHidMini XInput HID call site attempts report generation without a local equality guard. DMF generation success and lower HID read completion are separate observations.",
    "The inspected xinputhid ordinary read-completion path suppresses packet increment and queued delivery when its parser reports identical decoded state.",
    "The XInput mapper uses transformed stick axes, trigger pressure, buttons, hat, PS and battery; no motion fields or explicit per-report packet counter in this mapper.",
    "Repeated breakpoint hits alone do not establish unchanged successful completions or a pathological polling rate."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No new controller run; idle jitter remains a hypothesis.",
    "Source tag matches the installed release number; source-to-loaded-binary reproducibility was not independently verified.",
    "Raw HID report delivery and queued unfiltered-state completion are different layers.",
    "Native Xbox XUSB behavior was not inspected or measured here.",
    "Do not generalize this 18-byte decoded equality predicate to other xinputhid versions."
